comments.body:
The ZMQ settings are pulled from swss common via its `get_config()` method with keys `XPUB_END_KEY`, `XSUB_END_KEY`, `CAPTURE_END_KEY`.  These map, respectively, to strings `xpub_path`, `xsub_path`, and `capture_path`.

Theses values have defaults from `sonic-swss-common/common/events_common.cpp`:
```
const map_str_str_t cfg_default = {
    CFG_VAL(XSUB_END_KEY, "tcp://127.0.0.1:5570"),
    CFG_VAL(XPUB_END_KEY, "tcp://127.0.0.1:5571"),
    CFG_VAL(REQ_REP_END_KEY, "tcp://127.0.0.1:5572"),
    CFG_VAL(CAPTURE_END_KEY, "tcp://127.0.0.1:5573"),
    CFG_VAL(STATS_UPD_SECS, "5"),
    CFG_VAL(CACHE_MAX_CNT, "")
};
```

But are overwritten by values in `/etc/sonic/init_cfg.json` by default on the first call to `get_config()` (if the data isn't already populated).  It looks like a public function of `read_init_config(const char *init_cfg_file)` can be called before the first `get_config()` to read in an alternative file (say a temporary one with a unique name) which would prevent `/etc/sonic/init_cfg.json` from being read.   The parent object is named `events`.  An example file might look like:

```
{
  "events" : { 
     "xsub_path": "tcp://127.0.0.1:25570", 
     "xpub_path": "tcp://127.0.0.1:25571",
     "capture_path": "tcp://127.0.0.1:25573"
    }
}
```

The ports could also be randomly chosen if needed, but likely not a big deal.
